    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even if it feels minor, an allergic reaction could escalate quickly without proper attention. Reactions from even a tiny amount of an allergen like peanuts can sometimes vary in severity. Caffeine can indeed provide an energy boost, which might help you through your workout, but it's not advisable to rely on it to manage symptoms of an allergic reaction. The pre-workout powder generally energizes due to the caffeine content, but if you are in doubt, it would be safer to skip it to avoid any potential interaction with your allergy. It's crucial to prioritize your health, and an energy dip won't outweigh potentially serious consequences from an allergic reaction. Wait for a few hours to see how you adjust; if symptoms remain mild and stable, you might consider taking your pre-workout as usual, but only after you've made absolutely sure that it's safe for you. Consult with a health professional if you're unsure. Your well-being should always come first!",
